  SAM2ImageWrapper, get_modified_sam2 (including all their methods).
- src/utils.py inspected but no definitions are included: load_classes reads
  classes.json for unused upstream properties; inference gets names from YOLO.

Modifications:
- Extract only detection/segmentation; omit Streamlit, dotenv, cloud clients,
  VLM/OCR, topology/netlist generation, unrelated class maps and unused imports.
- Force CPU in construction/prediction and default model factory device.
- Use installed SAM-2 config registry names directly, without worktree chdir.
- Load fine-tuned state with explicit weights_only=True; initialization errors
  propagate instead of silently disabling SAM2. Segmentation keeps the original
  None-on-error result, which the worker rejects as failed inference.
- Worker imports these local modules, appends HCD geometry candidates, retains
  checkpoint hashes, restricted YOLO loading and manual correction API boundary.
- Preserve upstream refinement architecture (including its fixed 4 channels);
  checkpoint-compatible shapes and zero threshold are unchanged.

